// Bina OCR speed benchmark (2026-10-31 .. 2026-11-01).
//
// Why some pages were slow:
//  1. Repetition loops ("که که که ..."): the loop check only fired at the 2048-token cap (~8 s of junk),
//     then a hi-res retry looped at the same spot (~10 s), then the page was split and reread.
//  2. Dense Persian pages need 2.5k-4k tokens: they hit the 2048 cap with no loop, got the same useless retry, then split.
//  3. Decoding ~3.8 ms/token; half the GPU time went to the masked attention kernel (the mask never hides anything).
//
// Shipped:
//  - early loop stop: decoding.tail_loop / LoopStop, cuts a loop ~160 tokens after it starts. Text identical.
//  - token cap 2048 -> 4096 (server/ocr.py). Dense pages read in one pass. Persian CER unchanged (0%).
//  - unmasked decode steps, now the server default (?masked=1 = old decoding). ~1.75x per token.
//    Text changes on 5 of 21 pages (bf16 rounding, greedy decoding diverges): 0e better, 00 and en-serif-26-clean
//    get junk lines at the end, 11 and fa-naskh-22-clean differ by a word or two.
// Rejected: pre-splitting tall regions (hallucinated lines), SDPA enable_gqa (no speedup), skipping the hi-res retry (lost a line on 0e).
//
// Fields:
//  seconds            in-process ocr.transcribe time (no HTTP, no line boxes), model warm, one run each
//  model_calls        model.generate calls (retries and split halves count)
//  tokens             tokens generated across all calls
//  similarity_to_base difflib ratio of the text vs the "base" variant (real images have no ground truth)
//  cer_pct            character error rate vs the known text (synthetic pages, rendered with PIL; spaces/ZWNJ normalized)
//  http_baseline      first run through the live server's /v2/ocr before any change; it had a 30 s admin time limit,
//                     so 0e came back incomplete there
// Known: English synthetic pages have 11-44% CER in every variant (model emits fragments like `fad{i|},`): a quality issue, not speed.
// Images: real ones in ocr-test/; synthetic ones were generated for this run and are not in the repo.
{
  "date": "2026-11-01",
  "gpu": "NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090",
  "torch": "2.7.1+cu126",
  "transformers": "5.14.1",
  "shipped": {
    "default": "nomask,stop,cap4096",
    "masked=1": "stop,cap4096",
    "files": [
      "model/decoding.py",
      "model/hf_nemotron_parse_modeling.py",
      "server/ocr.py",
      "server/app.py"
    ]
  },
  "http_baseline": {
